{{also|đách}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|dach|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|Germanic|θakan|lang=de}}, compare Dutch {{term|dak|lang=nl}}. Cognate with Danish {{term|tag||roof|lang=da}}, English {{term|thack}}, Old Norse {{term|þak||thatch, roof|lang=non}}. Akin to Latin {{term|toga||garment}} and Ancient Greek {{term|στέγος|tr=stegos||roof|lang=grc}}.

